\f0\fs24 \cf0 The OBTAI_radiomics project has been implemented using Python v.3.11.13\
\
Prerequisites and Depedencies:\
Users should use a Python environment (Python v.3.11.13 recommended) in order to install the scientific and medical imaging packages as Pyradiomics, SimpleITK, Pandas, and Numpy.\
\
Directory Settings:\
\
Open the script and update the root path variables in STEP1 to match the local file structure:\
\
	\'93BASE_PATH_IMG\'94 : The path directory containing the normalized base images 3D-T1w+C.\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 	\'93BASE_PATH_MSK\'94: The path directory containing the three dimensional segmentation masks using the 3D-T1w+C images. Annotations adhere to the \'93nm\'94 schema described in the paper\
\
Execution:\
\
Run the script directly from your terminal within the configured environment.\
\
Function \'93_main_\'94 quantifies the radiomic features a set of 3D-T1w+C segmented MRIs in NIfTI format. This function reads image and segmentation input directories and save the radiomic features extracted in a CSV file. \
\
\
Input: \'93BASE_PATH_IMG\'94 : The path directory containing the normalized base images 3D-T1w+C.\
Input: \'93BASE_PATH_MSK\'94: The path directory containing the three dimensional segmentation masks using the 3D-T1w+C images.\
\
Output: \'93OUTPUT_CSV\'94: The path to the CSV file containing the radiomic features extracted separate comma-separated values. Recording each case, lesion and region in a row , and preserving the lesion tracking in the follow up.\
\
Output: \'93LOG_ERRORS\'94: The path to the .text file reporting the errors or warnings during the execution process.\
\
Monitoring:\
\
Incremental Output: The script automatically generates and updates OUTPUT_CSV. If interrupted, re-running the script will automatically detect existing records and resume execution from where it left off.\
\
Error Logging: Any missing files, structural warnings, or regions that do not fulfill the three dimensional filtering are recorded in LOG_ERRORS.}